{"id": "EUVD-2021-34885", "enisaUuid": "be2e410d-2107-33d6-91cc-2fe051b7cca3", "description": "fast-toml through 0.5.4 contains a prototype pollution vulnerability that allows attackers to modify Object.prototype by supplying TOML containing __proto__, constructor or prototype key segments. Attackers can pass [__proto__] or [constructor.prototype] table headers or __proto__.x dotted keys to parse() to pollute all objects, causing denial of service or authorization bypass.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T20:55:05", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Gin-Quin/fast-toml/issues/8", "https://github.com/Gin-Quin/fast-toml/pull/3", "https://github.com/Gin-Quin/fast-toml", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fast-toml-through-0.5.4-prototype-pollution-via-proto-keys-in-parsed-toml"], "aliases": ["CVE-2021-48012", "GHSA-qqfj-vf92-g76j"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c04c2529-0de4-3167-81d7-6d8d0848b9d3", "product": {"name": "fast-toml", "vendor": {"name": "Gin-Quin"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8249cb20-a78a-3fb0-83ec-4386f454250e", "vendor": {"name": "Gin-Quin"}}], "isExploited": false}